o share in the comments below  blazing fury Dollywood we couldn't have  thought of a better name ourselves but  Dollywood owned by ultimate country star  Dolly Parton yep that's right she owns  an amusement park we'll say it because  we know you're all thinking it it's  weird  however this park isn't as hunky-dory as  the name cracks it up to be on one of  their apparently child safe rides  entitled blazing fury a major injury was  sustained that resulted in a massive  lawsuit the ride is described as an  out-of-control fire just minutes away  from engulfed in the 1880s town yes you  heard right a man brought his family to  the park and sustained major brain  damage from the ride he is suing Dolly  Parton productions for twenty million  dollars it is a complicated case due to  the injuries but the park did not give  proper warning to the dangers the park  and the blazing fury Tour de France are  still open to this day so if you want to  visit a playground where rides and risk  could go hand-in-hand you can visit this  one today but we recommend you avoiding  a lawsuit and keeping that smart noggin  of yours intact  maybe dolly should have stuck to her  singing career and not ventured off into  children's amusements adventure  playground in Berkeley California  located in Berkeley California this  playground has been  written up as one of the ten best  playgrounds by National Geographic now  that's saying a lot so how did this park  in the pond our list of the most  dangerous would it be the nails lying  around on purpose or could it be these  slippery surfaces or even the zip line  what about the hammer in the saw this  park is touted as so incredibly great  because it gives children the  responsibility to build things and be  cautious when kids are confronted with  age-appropriate risks they are actually  more careful than when they can see they  are more advanced than what is given as  cool that the concept of this is there  are still dirty nails lying in the sand